  <revision rev="1" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>708eddac2f06a832d1eefc54c72b7fe1</srcmd5>
    <version>1.18.15</version>
    <time>1786461188</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>New package: opencode, an AI coding agent for the terminal.

Supersedes SR#1370389 for two fixes found while verifying the built package
in a Tumbleweed container:

* opencode-no-self-update.patch now also covers the explicit `opencode
  upgrade` command. Patch1 only guarded the automatic on-startup path; the
  CLI command reaches upstream's &quot;Install anyways?&quot; prompt (method() is
  &quot;unknown&quot; for an rpm-owned /usr/bin file) and blocks there, so the command
  never returns without a TTY. It now prints a pointer at the package manager
  and exits 0. OPENCODE_ENABLE_AUTOUPDATE=1 still restores upstream
  behaviour.

* The SIGILL in the bundled opentui core is fixed by SR#1370419, which
  supersedes #1370385 - opencode links libopentui.so and crashed on older
  aarch64 before that.

Verified in a Tumbleweed container: deps resolve, --version/--help/models/
providers/agent/stats/debug all work, models resolves offline from the
embedded catalogue, the HTTP API serves /doc, /config, /session and /agent,
uninstall is a no-op on a packaged install, and the TUI renders and takes
keyboard input. Local build green on aarch64; rpmlint 0 errors, 1 warning
(position-independent-executable-suggested, inherent to bun --compile),
0 badness.

Still needs bun (SR#1370367) and opentui (SR#1370419) staged alongside it.</comment>
    <requestid>1370420</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>9810785777b0cbcf7af115428bb4b219</srcmd5>
    <version>1.18.18</version>
    <time>1786826481</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Update to version 1.18.18

Model/provider handling fixes (Kimi and Muse system prompt routing, xai
xhigh reasoning effort, reasoning effort passthrough for groq/mistral/xai,
DeepSeek V4 Flash sampling defaults, Merge Gateway reasoning effort),
compaction that keeps recent turns whole, capped and jittered automatic
retries, PDF attachments for Copilot models advertising PDF vision, and
unknown top-level config fields no longer failing the whole config file.

Also hardens the shipped opencode_vendor helper - none of it changes the
binary that gets built: install with --cpu/--os set to all platforms so the
x86_64 natives survive a vendor regeneration done on aarch64, keep
node_modules/dist/ts-dist out of the slimmed tarball at any nesting depth,
and ship patches/ which package.json and bun.lock reference by path for 17
patched dependencies.

Licence audit redone for this version: 506 of 507 vendored packages declare
a licence, none copyleft; poe-oauth 0.0.8 declares none. Recorded in the
Legal-Review-Notice in the spec.

Built locally on aarch64 and on OBS for x86_64; %check reports 1.18.18 on
both. rpmlint: 0 errors, 0 badness, 1 warning
(position-independent-executable-suggested, unavoidable for a
bun build --compile executable).</comment>
    <requestid>1371300</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>0909c4ffad4d476086941c605f278bbd</srcmd5>
    <version>1.18.19</version>
    <time>1787324011</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Thu Aug 20 18:47:55 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal &lt;mpluskal@suse.com&gt;

- Update to version 1.18.19:
  * Cloudflare AI Gateway models get native OpenAI and Anthropic
    passthroughs, Codex rate limits match ChatGPT subscriptions,
    and ChatGPT workspace compute residency is forwarded.
  * Drop built-in Qwen sampling defaults that could send
    unsupported settings, ignore malformed model prices instead of
    breaking cost calculation, and fall back when OpenAI websocket
    requests exceed the message size limit.
  * /connect lists authenticated providers, the default Console URL
    is updated, web search works with the OpenCode Go provider, and
    v1 session databases stay readable.
  * Grep previews keep unicode characters.
- Retrace the vendor keep list (508 to 509 store entries). The SPDX
  license set is unchanged and still contains no copyleft.
- Reverse opencode-relax-bun-version.patch after --retrace so
  Source0 stays the upstream tree and Patch0 still applies at
  %prep.</comment>
    <requestid>1372626</requestid>
